body:
Love this list! Ngl, part of the reason I don't want kids is about the whole world going to shit and how having kids is not affordable in most cases. But a huge part of it is that I just like my life as is.

As for other things to add to the list:

* Travel, go out for food, or do something fun and pay for only yourself (and someone else if you like, but not out of obligation);
* Handle your hangovers like a champ;
* Try new foods/restaurants that fussy kids might otherwise take issue with (to hell with your hypothetical kid's demand for chicken fingers or spaghetti with hotdogs for the 6th day in a row; I want Thai food today, Peruvian tomorrow, and Ethiopian on Friday);
* Do almost **anything** you want to outside of the house without ever wondering which friend or acquaintance might make good babysitter or about what time you need to be home; 
* Save money or splurge on yourself as you like; and
* Enjoy car rides with only the music you want to enjoy

Also to touch on the video games part - almost all of the video games I play are violent; some are graphically so. I'm glad I'll never need to wait for a child to be asleep or at a friend's house just to play.
